# kitchen_sink

Native bindings for kitchen_sink

Node.js bindings for the `kitchen_sink` native library: an ES module over a small N-API addon (`kitchen_sink_node.c`). `npm install` uses a prebuilt addon when one matches the platform (from a per-platform package, or under `prebuilds/<os>-<cpu>/`) and otherwise compiles it with node-gyp. A compiled addon links `kitchen_sink`; set `KITCHEN_SINK_LIBRARY` to the library file (or its directory) when installing, or pass `--kitchen_sink-library=<path>` to npm.

```sh
KITCHEN_SINK_LIBRARY=/path/to/libkitchen_sink.so npm install kitchen_sink
```

Each top-level module of the API is a namespace export:

```js
import { shared, kitchen } from 'kitchen_sink';
```

